CFzoSAcCHid-R4oj-7","textSize":16,"rotation":351},{"id":"5WKjkgvCZLrSnkysi2YK7","fillColor":"#3f51b5","height":120,"position":{"x":9800,"y":5580},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":120,"text":"next steps collection and structuring","attachedFrame":"y5fCFzoSAcCHid-R4oj-7","textSize":16,"rotation":351},{"id":"TsLIYX6mKvsd55h0afln2","fillColor":"#cd93d7","height":120,"position":{"x":9960,"y":5520},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":120,"text":"frontend trouble-shooting ","attachedFrame":"y5fCFzoSAcCHid-R4oj-7","textSize":16},{"id":"xzyfjKtEVWp-yTovcO9MI","fillColor":"#ffffff","height":120,"position":{"x":9900,"y":5660},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":120,"text":"timeline and meetings for next year","attachedFrame":"y5fCFzoSAcCHid-R4oj-7","textSize":16,"rotation":6},{"id":"_7X2Nmv9PX9znY7Fd5byZ","fillColor":"#8d6bc9","height":120,"position":{"x":10040,"y":5700},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":120,"text":"conference  participation confirmation","attachedFrame":"y5fCFzoSAcCHid-R4oj-7","textSize":16,"rotation":355},{"id":"giXTaafJCIKh9H1zOpBFs","type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","position":{"x":10720,"y":4860},"width":1720,"height":120,"fillColor":"#607d8b","text":"Methodenbeschreibung","textFontFamily":"Inter","textAlignment":"left","attachedFrame":"D69SRHxSzMYncdRrTkhbm","textSize":56,"textColor":"#ffffff","textBold":true},{"id":"oPoL2nQKKrpoR47N_oNqD","type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","position":{"x":10740,"y":5030},"width":1680,"height":885,"fillColor":"transparent","text":"💡 Beispiel: Retrospektive im Einsatz\n\n🎯 Wofür: Dieses Board zeigt eine abgeschlossene Retrospektive. Nutzen Sie es, um neuen Teams das Format zu erklären.\n\n1. Felder lesen\nCONTINUE: Was gut lief. STOP: Was bremst. INVENT: Neue Ideen. ACT: Konkrete nächste Schritte.\n\n2. Muster erkennen\nAchten Sie darauf, wie Probleme aus STOP in ACT zu Aufgaben werden, z. B. „endless meetings\" → „timeline and meetings for next year\".\n\n3. Selbst anwenden\nStarten Sie mit der leeren Vorlage „Retrospektive\" und nutzen Sie dieses Beispiel als Orientierung.\n\n🛠️ Ihre Rolle als Moderator\nErklärer: Zeigen Sie das Beispiel vor der ersten Retro eines Teams.\nMutmacher: Machen Sie deutlich, dass kurze Karten völlig ausreichen.","textFontFamily":"Inter","textAlignment":"left","attachedFrame":"D69SRHxSzMYncdRrTkhbm","textSize":30,"textColor":"#000000"}]}]}}